🧠 Tips
- Use ../ to go up one folder level.
- Use defer in your <script> tag to ensure the script runs after the HTML is parsed.
- Keep your CSS and JS in centralized folders like /css and /js to avoid duplication.


Subject of the Website:
Future Child Sportive
Planned Content of the Website:
The homepage (index.html) will introduce Future Child Sportive, a youth-focused initiative that promotes physical fitness, 
teamwork, and personal development through sports. 
The page will highlight the mission and vision of the program, showcase featured sports activities 
(like football, athletics, and basketball), and include testimonials from participants and parents. 
It will also provide a brief overview of upcoming events and a call-to-action for parents to enroll their children or support 
the initiative. The site will include navigation to other pages such as About and Contact, 
and a footer with references and social links.


Reason for Choosing This Subject:
I chose this subject because I believe in the power of sports to shape confident, disciplined, 
and healthy children. Future Child Sportive represents a vision for nurturing the next generation through structured 
physical activity and community engagement. 
Creating this website is a way to share that vision and inspire others to support youth development 
through sports.






